smartinit.v3.2.5
Q3FY14 Downscaling Implementation

- Hourly output for CONUS2p5 from 0-36 hours (wave modeling request)
- Improved diagnostic wind model to account for terrain
- dgex conus and alaska domain downscaling 

===================================================================================
1.  DGEX DOWN-SCALING (NET=DGEX, RUN=DGEX)

NOTE:  DGEX smartinit depends on completion of SREFTOGEFS SREFPROB file thru 192 hours 
       from SREF Network run.
       NAM downscaling SREFPROB file are already available thru 84 hours.

        Final SREF GENS product (mean, spread, prob) files on SREF GRID have been extended to
        192 forecast hour by SREF team for dgex downscaling.
        Therefore, each DGEX 3 hr downscaling processing will depend on the following sref files:
        /com/sref/prod/sref.yyyymmdd/ensprod_gefs/{CYC}
            sref.t{CYC}z.pgrb{GRD}.{prbtyp}_3hrly.grib 
where
  prbtyp=mean,max,min,mod,spread,prob,p10,p25,p50,p75 or p90
  FILE SIZE = 5 MB/file

===================================================================================
1A. Additional SREF and DGEX post-processing
===================================================================================

Additional jobs are needed to extend SREF GEFS look-alike files from 90 to 192 forecast hours.
This requires additional tasks for MPMD jobs described below

The SREF team will provide jobs that are triggered once the GEFS 21 member sig files thru 192 forecast hours are available.
(by arount +2:30 hours after cycle time for 03,09,15,21 UTC SREF runs)
These jobs and scripts perform the same tasks (with the same names) that are
currently run as part of the SREF system through 90 forecast hours 4x/day.

#********************************************************************************************************
NOTE: These gefs2sref jobs will be run as part of the SREF system upgrade for smartinit downscaling.
#********************************************************************************************************


========================================================================
1B.  JDGEX_SMINIT   --> downscale dgex jobs 
=========================================================================
ECF additional dgex smartinit jobs:  Run every 3 hrs to 192 DGEX forecast hours 
NCO should run JDGEX_SMINIT every 3 forecast hours beginning with the DGEX start hour 
and ending at DGEX forecast hour 192.
The downscaling is run once the dgex bsmart files are available.  Otherwise, run as is done
for NAM smartinit ecflow processing.
In ecf dir:
  ~/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jdgex_sminit_conus_fHH.ecf (HH=78,81...192)   CYCLE 06/18 UTC
  ~/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jdgex_sminit_ak_fHH.ecf (HH=84,93..192)      CYCLE 00/12 UTC

JOBS (/jobs):       JDGEX_SMINIT
SCRIPTS (/scripts): jdgex_smartinit.sh.ecf
USH (/ush):         jdgex_smartinit.sh

Additional parm  prdgen control files
  ../parm/dgex_masterak.ctl
  ../parm/dgex_masterconus.ctl

Additional fix wgt prdgen files
 ../fix/wgt/dgex_wgt_197_conus   (interp to 5 km grid 197)
../fix/wgt/dgex_wgt_198_alaska    (interp to 5 km grid 198)
=============================================================================================

Once the jsref_gefs2sref.ecf ecf job is complete from the SREF Network, 
the smartinit system (JDGEX_SMINIT) can be run with: 

export RUNTYP=dgex_ak --->  for downscaling to Alaska 5 km grid at cycles 00/12 UTC  
(smartinit invoked from ECFlow every 3 hrs for forecast hours 84-->192)

export RUNTYP=dgex_cs --->  for downscaling to CONUS 5 km grid at cycles 06/18 UTC   
(smartinit invoked from ECFLOW every 3 hrs for forecast hours 78-->192)


INPUT: dgex bsmart files

***OUTPUT: dgex.t{06/18}z.smartconus{HHH}.tm00 (or grib2) from forecast hours 78 thru 192
90-130 MB per 3 hr forecast hour
3 wall clock mins/forecast hr

***OUTPUT: dgex.t{00/12}z.smartak{HHH}.tm00 (or grib2)      from forecast hours 84 thru 192
45-64 MB per 3 hr forecast hour
2 wall clock mins/forecast hr

AWIPS: Only HAINES INDEX will be transferred to AWIPS for DNG DGEX.
DGEX WMO Header AWIPS files will be provided by NCO.


========================================================================
2.  NAM Smartinit upgrade
========================================================================

The primary change is to implement a diagnostic wind field model to more accurately account for terrain effectfor the high resolution downscaled grids.
Also if file space is available, the nam conus2p5 smartinit downscaled hourly output would be extended from 12 to 36 hours and then output 3 hourly after that.


